Package: rism
Type: Package
Title: Radiomic Feature Integration with Spike-and-Slab for Multimodal Survival Analysis
Version: 0.2.1
Authors@R: person("Sagnik", "Bhadury", email = "bhadury@umich.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Group selection for the Cox proportional hazards model when
    predictors come in groups (e.g. principal component scores of a tumor
    boundary or of an intensity density from one imaging sequence). Two methods
    are provided. Group BMA enumerates the group-inclusion models (or searches
    them by Markov chain Monte Carlo model composition) with a point-mass
    spike, a Gaussian slab, Laplace-approximated marginal likelihoods of the
    partial likelihood, a beta-binomial prior on the number of groups and an
    empirical-Bayes slab variance. Grouped SS samples a continuous grouped
    spike-and-slab prior by Metropolis-Hastings within Gibbs. Both return
    posterior inclusion probabilities per group and posterior summaries of the
    coefficients; pre-validated risk scores and a permutation reference for the
    inclusion probabilities are provided for Group BMA.
